econet-eth: distinguish pre-GRO skb fragments and count flowtable commits

The pre-GRO handoff proved that GRO fraglists are no longer involved, but
modern mac80211 deliberately keeps most A-MSDU payload in page fragments.
Expose separate frag_list, nr_frags and maximum-nr_frags counters so that this
hardware limit is visible without packet logging.

Also account successful flowtable RX commits in the existing RX_COMMIT
diagnostic.  The commit was previously visible only through rate-limited trace
messages, leaving the summary counter at zero.

